result = await orchestrator.render(url, readiness_selector="[data-product-price]")
# Returns fully rendered DOM with price loaded</code></pre>
<p>The selector <em>[data-product-price]</em> ensures the price has loaded before extraction. Without it, the pipeline might extract before the API call completes.</p>

<h3>Example 2: Infinite Scroll Feed</h3>
<p>A news feed that loads articles in batches as the user scrolls.</p>
<pre><code>async def render_with_scroll(url, scroll_count=3, scroll_delay=2000):
    page = await ctx.new_page()
    await page.goto(url, wait_until='networkidle')
    for i in range(scroll_count):
        await page.evaluate('window.scrollTo(0, document.body.scrollHeight)')
        await page.wait_for_timeout(scroll_delay)
        await page.wait_for_load_state('networkidle')
    return await page.content()</code></pre>

